    {
      "name": "every other ask at the old door meets silence",
      "law": "Rotation",
      "obligations": ["XIII-4"],
      "derivation": "The new holder asks the being itself for something. Article XIII: \"Every other ask meets silence: an answer's data is the field's declared answer type by the notation's rules, and a succession is not that type, so the old door cannot put one where the caller asked for something else.\" So this is silence and not the succession, and not an absent answer either — the door has the succession and may not hand it back under a field that declared something else. The number is still spent, the message having arrived and been judged.",
